---
title: "user_data_access (kintai-v3: Initial Schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: user authenticates via Supabase Auth
    q_auth --> q_operation: determine operation type

    q_operation --> q_select: SELECT on users
    q_operation --> q_update: UPDATE on users

    q_select --> q_sel_own: auth.uid() = id
    q_select --> q_sel_admin: is_admin() = true
    q_sel_own --> q_return_rows: return matching rows
    q_sel_admin --> q_return_rows: return all matching rows
    q_select --> q_sel_deny: auth.uid() != id AND is_admin() = false

    q_update --> q_upd_own: auth.uid() = id (USING and WITH CHECK)
    q_update --> q_upd_admin: is_admin() = true (USING and WITH CHECK)
    q_upd_own --> q_apply_update: apply field changes
    q_upd_admin --> q_apply_update: apply field changes
    q_update --> q_upd_deny: auth.uid() != id AND is_admin() = false

    q_apply_update --> q_return_rows: update successful
    q_sel_deny --> q_deny: operation denied
    q_upd_deny --> q_deny: operation denied

    q_return_rows --> [*]: return result
    q_deny --> [*]: RLS violation

    note right of q_select
        INV-001: Users can only SELECT their own row (auth.uid() = id)
        INV-002: Admins can SELECT all user rows
        INV-003: No INSERT policy exists - user creation is server-side only
    end note

    note right of q_update
        INV-004: Users can UPDATE only their own row (both USING and WITH CHECK enforce auth.uid() = id)
        INV-005: Admins can UPDATE any user row
        INV-006: No DELETE policy - users cannot be deleted via client
    end note
